# Without this, `COPY . .` in the builder stage (Dockerfile) drags host files in
# on top of the ones the image just built:
#
#   - node_modules/ overwrites the container's Linux-built copy. On a macOS or
#     Windows host that ships a darwin/win32 better-sqlite3 binary and the
#     container dies on require. This is the most common "works on my machine"
#     break in the kit, because the README quickstart is
#     clone -> npm install -> docker compose up.
#   - .env (real Stripe/Litestream secrets) and data/app.db (password hashes)
#     land in a build layer, where they stay readable in image history long
#     after the file is gone from the working tree.
#
# The DB is supplied at runtime by the ./data bind mount in docker-compose.yml,
# and the runner stage creates /app/data itself, so nothing is lost here.

node_modules
.next
.git
.gitignore

data
.env
.env*.local

# Generated / typecheck artifacts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not needed to build or run; the runner copies only .next, public,
# node_modules, package.json and scripts out of the builder.
tests
drizzle
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
README.md
LICENSE
